  {
   "identifier": "p-text",
   "id": "doc-1jjc290gv0",
   "content": {
    "text": "<strong>You can only read this in the NZZ:</strong> The expectations for the office of the German Federal President are exceptionally high. The officeholder is expected to inspire the country and deliver bold, rousing speeches. Finding such a personality is challenging enough. Now, the successor to incumbent Frank-Walter Steinmeier is also expected to be a woman for the first time, and a bulwark against the right. Both requirements are ill-conceived. <a href=\"https://www.nzz.ch/ld.10021076\">To the commentary</a>"
   },
   "data": {},
